; HomerView.jsd -- what the Key Describer says about each command
;
; Present tense, one sentence, and where the key is not obvious the sentence
; says why it is that key.

hVCheckAccessibility=Check Accessibility
hVCheckAccessibility_Synopsis=Tests the page for accessibility problems and says how many were found. A for Accessibility.
hVCheckAccessibility_Description=Press Alt+JAWSKey+A. Tests the page for accessibility problems and says how many were found. A for Accessibility.
hVDescribeLinkTarget=Link Target
hVDescribeLinkTarget_Synopsis=Shows the address of the link under the cursor and what is at it, without going there: what kind of thing, how big, and whether it ends up where it claims. L for Link.
hVDescribeLinkTarget_Description=Press Alt+L. Shows the address of the link under the cursor and what is at it, without going there: what kind of thing, how big, and whether it ends up where it claims. L for Link.
hVExtractMainContent=Extract Main Content
hVExtractMainContent_Synopsis=Extracts the readable part of the page into a tab of its own. F9 is Edge's own reading view, and Shift+F9 is HomerView's, which works on pages Edge will not.
hVExtractMainContent_Description=Press Shift+F9. Extracts the readable part of the page into a tab of its own. F9 is Edge's own reading view, and Shift+F9 is HomerView's, which works on pages Edge will not.
hVLaunchHomerView=Launch HomerView
hVLaunchHomerView_Synopsis=Launches or reconnects HomerView's copy of Microsoft Edge. H for HomerView, and it works anywhere because nothing is running yet.
hVLaunchHomerView_Description=Press Alt+JAWSKey+H. Launches or reconnects HomerView's copy of Microsoft Edge. H for HomerView, and it works anywhere because nothing is running yet.
hVMoveToProbableMain=Jump to Probable Main
hVMoveToProbableMain_Synopsis=Moves to the first main content, or probable main content, of which a page should have only one -- whether the page declares it or not, weighing every part of the page when it does not. Shift+Q, beside JAWS's own Q, because a page has one main region and the native Shift+Q -- the previous one -- has nowhere to go.
hVMoveToProbableMain_Description=Press Shift+Q. Moves to the first main content, or probable main content, of which a page should have only one -- whether the page declares it or not, weighing every part of the page when it does not. Shift+Q, beside JAWS's own Q, because a page has one main region and the native Shift+Q -- the previous one -- has nowhere to go.
hVShowHomerViewMenu_Synopsis=Lists every HomerView command, whether or not it has a key of its own, so nothing is hidden behind a keystroke you have to know.
hVShowHomerViewMenu_Description=Opens the HomerView menu. Arrow through the commands and press Enter on one. The same key as the Alternate Menu on the NVDA side.
hVCopyLogToClipboard_Synopsis=Puts HomerView's JAWS log on the clipboard as a file, ready to attach to a message with Control+V.
hVCopyLogToClipboard_Description=The log records every command sent to the browser and anything that failed. This copies the file itself where Windows allows it, so Control+V in an Outlook message attaches it, and the path as text otherwise.
hVCopyPageLinks_Synopsis=Puts the text and address of every link on the page on the clipboard, one per line.
hVCopyPageLinks_Description=A page's links are a table of contents nobody prints. This copies them so they can be pasted, searched or kept.
hVDismissDialog_Synopsis=Closes cookie banners, newsletter offers and anything else covering the page.
hVDismissDialog_Description=Closes open dialogs, presses the close button where there is one, and removes whatever else is pinned over the content. Says how many things it shifted.
hVListTabs_Synopsis=Lists the open tabs by name and address.
hVListTabs_Description=On the Alternate Menu only. F4, which the NVDA side uses, puts the cursor in this browser's address bar.
hVOpenUserGuide_Synopsis=Opens the HomerView guide.
hVOpenUserGuide_Description=Control+F1 on a web page, and on the Alternate Menu everywhere. Not a global key, because Control+F1 collapses the ribbon in Office.
hVSayMetadata_Synopsis=Shows what the page says about itself: title, author, publisher, dates, summary, licence and language.
hVSayMetadata_Description=Reports where each answer came from, because a date from a citation tag and one guessed from a time element are not equally trustworthy.
hVHotKeyHelp_Synopsis=Lists every HomerView command and its key, including those with no key at all.
hVHotKeyHelp_Description=Also says which things JAWS already does, so HomerView does not.
hVSayClipboard=Say Clipboard
hVSayClipboard_Synopsis=Says what is on the clipboard: the paths when files have been copied, the text otherwise. The apostrophe is a quotation mark, and a clipboard holds a quotation.
hVSayClipboard_Description=Press Alt+Apostrophe. Says what is on the clipboard: the paths when files have been copied, the text otherwise. The apostrophe is a quotation mark, and a clipboard holds a quotation.
hVSaveClipboard=Save Clipboard
hVSaveClipboard_Synopsis=Saves the clipboard to a text file, proposing the last name used.
hVSaveClipboard_Description=Press Control+Apostrophe. Saves the clipboard to a text file, proposing the last name used.
hVAppendClipboard=Append Clipboard
hVAppendClipboard_Synopsis=Adds the clipboard to the end of a text file rather than replacing it.
hVAppendClipboard_Description=Press Control+Shift+Apostrophe. Adds the clipboard to the end of a text file rather than replacing it.
hVClearClipboard=Clear Clipboard
hVClearClipboard_Synopsis=Empties the clipboard, so an append starts afresh.
hVClearClipboard_Description=Press Alt+Shift+Apostrophe. Empties the clipboard, so an append starts afresh.
hVStartSelection=Start Selection
hVStartSelection_Synopsis=Marks where a selection begins. Move to the end and press Shift+F8. Drops JAWS's temporary placemarker, which is the mechanism a virtual buffer actually uses. A pair rather than a drag, so a passage longer than a screen can be selected.
hVStartSelection_Description=Press F8. Marks where a selection begins. Move to the end and press Shift+F8. Drops JAWS's temporary placemarker, which is the mechanism a virtual buffer actually uses. A pair rather than a drag, so a passage longer than a screen can be selected.
hVCompleteSelection=Complete Selection
hVCompleteSelection_Synopsis=Selects from where F8 was pressed to here, and says how much.
hVCompleteSelection_Description=Press Shift+F8. Selects from where F8 was pressed to here, and says how much.
hVCopySelection=Copy Selection
hVCopySelection_Synopsis=Copies what is selected, or the line under the cursor when nothing is. Edge copies a selection and nothing without one; this does both.
hVCopySelection_Description=Press Control+C. Copies what is selected, or the line under the cursor when nothing is. Edge copies a selection and nothing without one; this does both.
hVCopyAppend=Copy Append
hVCopyAppend_Synopsis=Adds what is selected, or the current line, to what is already on the clipboard, for gathering several passages into one note.
hVCopyAppend_Description=Press Alt+C. Adds what is selected, or the current line, to what is already on the clipboard, for gathering several passages into one note.
hVCopyAll=Copy All
hVCopyAll_Synopsis=Puts the whole page on the clipboard as text. JAWS has no equivalent: selecting a virtual document and copying it takes the browser's selection, which on many pages brings the navigation and the footers with it.
hVCopyAll_Description=Press Control+F8. Puts the whole page on the clipboard as text. JAWS has no equivalent: selecting a virtual document and copying it takes the browser's selection, which on many pages brings the navigation and the footers with it.
hVReadAll=Read All
hVReadAll_Synopsis=Speaks the whole page from the top and leaves the cursor where it was. Say All speaks the virtual view from the cursor onward and moves it; this speaks the page's own text, which is what Control+A would select.
hVReadAll_Description=Press Alt+F8. Speaks the whole page from the top and leaves the cursor where it was. Say All speaks the virtual view from the cursor onward and moves it; this speaks the page's own text, which is what Control+A would select.
hVCheckAccessibilityIbm=Check Accessibility with IBM
hVCheckAccessibilityIbm_Synopsis=Runs IBM Equal Access, whose unified ruleset folds EN 301 549 and Section 508 in with WCAG, and saves the results in every format to a folder named after the page under Downloads. I for IBM.
hVCheckAccessibilityIbm_Description=Press Alt+JAWSKey+I. Runs IBM Equal Access, whose unified ruleset folds EN 301 549 and Section 508 in with WCAG, and saves the results in every format to a folder named after the page under Downloads. I for IBM.
hVOpenDocument=Open Document
hVOpenDocument_Synopsis=Opens a Word file, PDF, ebook, spreadsheet or slide deck as a web page, so every HomerView command works on it. Control+O opens a file in every browser; this opens more kinds.
hVOpenDocument_Description=Press Control+O. Opens a Word file, PDF, ebook, spreadsheet or slide deck as a web page, so every HomerView command works on it. Control+O opens a file in every browser; this opens more kinds.
hVSavePage=Save Page
hVSavePage_Synopsis=Saves this page as html, or as anything pandoc can write, chosen by naming the file. Control+S saves in every browser; this saves more ways.
hVSavePage_Description=Press Control+S. Saves this page as html, or as anything pandoc can write, chosen by naming the file. Control+S saves in every browser; this saves more ways.
hVDownloadFiles=Web Download
hVDownloadFiles_Synopsis=Fetches the files a page links to, using the browser's own cookies, user agent and referrer so a gated file comes as it would to a click. Alt+Shift+W, EdSharp's key for it.
hVDownloadFiles_Description=Press Alt+Shift+W. Fetches the files a page links to, using the browser's own cookies, user agent and referrer so a gated file comes as it would to a click. Alt+Shift+W, EdSharp's key for it.
hVOpenPageFolder=Page Folder
hVOpenPageFolder_Synopsis=Opens this page's folder in File Explorer, so the files saved from it can be browsed. Nothing is created: if nothing has been saved from this page, it says so. Alt+Shift+F, beside Alt+Shift+W which fills the folder.
hVOpenPageFolder_Description=Press Alt+Shift+F. Opens this page's folder in File Explorer, so the files saved from it can be browsed. Nothing is created: if nothing has been saved from this page, it says so. Alt+Shift+F, beside Alt+Shift+W which fills the folder.
hVSayDiagnostics=Diagnostics
hVSayDiagnostics_Synopsis=Says whether the helper program, the log folder and the start page are where they should be, in speech, without writing a log or calling the helper. If HomerView does nothing at all, press this first.
hVSayDiagnostics_Description=Press Alt+JAWSKey+Q. Says whether the helper program, the log folder and the start page are where they should be, in speech, without writing a log or calling the helper. If HomerView does nothing at all, press this first.
hVSayTabNames=Tab Names
hVSayTabNames_Synopsis=Says the names of the open tabs and moves nothing. Tab List is for going somewhere; this is for knowing what is open.
hVSayTabNames_Description=Press Shift+F4. Says the names of the open tabs and moves nothing. Tab List is for going somewhere; this is for knowing what is open.
hVOpenQuickStart=Quick Start
hVOpenQuickStart_Synopsis=The short introduction to HomerView, opened in HomerView's own browser.
hVOpenQuickStart_Description=Press Alt+Shift+F1. The short introduction to HomerView, opened in HomerView's own browser.
hVShowHistory=History of Changes
hVShowHistory_Synopsis=What changed in each release.
hVShowHistory_Description=Press Shift+F1. What changed in each release.
hVOpenDeveloperNotes=Developer Notes
hVOpenDeveloperNotes_Synopsis=Notes for anyone working on HomerView itself.
hVOpenDeveloperNotes_Description=Press Control+Shift+F1. Notes for anyone working on HomerView itself.
hVOpenAnnouncement=Project Announcement
hVOpenAnnouncement_Synopsis=What HomerView is for, in its own words.
hVOpenAnnouncement_Description=On the Alternate Menu. What HomerView is for, in its own words.
hVOpenSessionLog=Session Log
hVOpenSessionLog_Synopsis=Opens this session's log to read, where Log to Clipboard copies it to send.
hVOpenSessionLog_Description=Press Alt+Control+F1. Opens this session's log to read, where Log to Clipboard copies it to send.
hVShowAbout=About HomerView
hVShowAbout_Synopsis=Which build is loaded, when it was installed, and where the program and the log live.
hVShowAbout_Description=Press Alt+F1. Which build is loaded, when it was installed, and where the program and the log live.
hVFindBackwards=Reverse Find for Text
hVFindBackwards_Synopsis=Searches backwards for text. JAWS's own Control+F searches forward only; this is the half it has no key for.
hVFindBackwards_Description=Press Control+Shift+F. Searches backwards for text. JAWS's own Control+F searches forward only; this is the half it has no key for.
hVFindByPattern=Forward Find with Regular Expression
hVFindByPattern_Synopsis=Searches forward for a pattern, which JAWS's own find cannot do.
hVFindByPattern_Description=Press Control+F3. Searches forward for a pattern, which JAWS's own find cannot do.
hVFindByPatternBackwards=Reverse Find with Regular Expression
hVFindByPatternBackwards_Synopsis=Searches backwards for a pattern.
hVFindByPatternBackwards_Description=Press Control+Shift+F3. Searches backwards for a pattern.
hVFindNext=Forward Find Again
hVFindNext_Synopsis=The next match, of whichever kind of find was done last.
hVFindNext_Description=Press F3. The next match, of whichever kind of find was done last.
hVFindPrevious=Reverse Find Again
hVFindPrevious_Synopsis=The previous match, of whichever kind of find was done last.
hVFindPrevious_Description=Press Shift+F3. The previous match, of whichever kind of find was done last.
hVExtractByPattern=Extract with Regular Expression
hVExtractByPattern_Synopsis=Gathers every match of a pattern for reading, separated by a form feed between blank lines.
hVExtractByPattern_Description=Press Control+Shift+E. Gathers every match of a pattern for reading, separated by a form feed between blank lines.
hVFindContacts=Find Contacts
hVFindContacts_Synopsis=Finds who to tell about this site: email addresses, the accessibility statement, contact pages and social media. Looks at this page, the home page, and the addresses a statement usually lives at.
hVFindContacts_Description=Press Alt+JAWSKey+C. Finds who to tell about this site: email addresses, the accessibility statement, contact pages and social media. Looks at this page, the home page, and the addresses a statement usually lives at.
hVCopyLogToClipboard=Log to Clipboard
hVCopyLogToClipboard_Synopsis=Puts the HomerView log on the clipboard as a file, so Control+V attaches it to a message rather than typing its name into one.
hVCopyPageLinks=Page Links to Clipboard
hVCopyPageLinks_Synopsis=Copies every link address on the page to the clipboard, as EdSharp copies a path on the same key.
hVDismissDialog=Dismiss Dialog
hVDismissDialog_Synopsis=Closes a cookie banner, newsletter offer or consent wall that Escape will not.
hVListTabs=Tab List
hVListTabs_Synopsis=Lists the HomerView tabs as links and switches to the one you choose.
hVOpenUserGuide=User Guide
hVOpenUserGuide_Synopsis=Opens the HomerView guide in the HomerView window.
hVSayMetadata=Say Metadata
hVSayMetadata_Synopsis=Says what the page claims about itself: author, publisher, date and licence.
hVShowHomerViewMenu=Alternate Menu
hVShowHomerViewMenu_Synopsis=Presents every command in one list with its key beside it. Nothing in HomerView is hidden behind a key you must know first.
hVHotKeyHelp=Hotkey Summary
hVHotKeyHelp_Synopsis=Shows every command and key in a window where each key is a link, and gives the version and install time on its first line.
hVListNames=List Names
hVListNames_Synopsis=Lists the people, places, organisations, dates and amounts a page mentions, saved as Names.htm in the page's folder and opened. A rule-based engine reads the text, so it guesses; the report says so.
hVListNames_Description=Press Alt+N. Lists the people, places, organisations, dates and amounts a page mentions, saved as Names.htm in the page's folder and opened. A rule-based engine reads the text, so it guesses; the report says so.
